:{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9e7a8c305b5d58e33ba473e18e7e4ff561a38e52.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The silicon transistor shown in figure below has <img src=\"/media/b8f155a93e7799b89f5e4cf2adeff52e9df5ebbb.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = 0.5 μA, <em>V<sub>BE</sub></em> = 0.7 V and β = 75 at room temperature and VBE has a temperature coefficient of –2 mV/°C. Then what is the value of <img src=\"/media/83ff0b17969afc860940da85951f0dbdd70a9fb7.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> if the temperature rises by 20°C? Assume β to be constant.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d806c282a5783bcd2337a16202fc67271480363f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2 mA</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1.5 mA</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 3.24 mA</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 5 mA</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/6ee68e1e7219156124498ca688c1cfac8dc8eb93.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/6860c952a650fd824e277a3402baaea2e631c5c5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The circuit in the figure utilizes three identical diodes having η = 1 and <img src=\"/media/e5c35bfdd83d71e50ec45c61b6b4182f829fe66f.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = 10–14 A. Then the value of the current <img src=\"/media/0eaa0592132083b589863945dc3fe69341ee6c79.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> required to obtain voltage <em>V</em><sub>o</sub> = 2 V is ________ mA. (Take, <em>V<sub>T</sub></em> = 25 mV) (Rounded off to one decimal place)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/4d55e2485eeb4f8a809ea0ea51efba45d6926071.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3.8","high":"3.8"},"solution":"<p>3.8 (3.7 - 3.9)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/3be71dea4c07518c56ef24ae33e4e973ca368fb6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The circuit shown in figure is a model for a battery charger. Here, <img src=\"/media/69fc756707526cdd396bdf5cf72080cd3a4df497.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is a 10 V peak sine wave, <em>D</em><sub>1 </sub>and <em>D<sub>2</sub></em> are ideal diodes, <img src=\"/media/4e68c0e8355e361a5e61e0d3c3af2f0db4ce4ce8.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is 100 mA current source and <em>B</em> is a 4.5 V battery. If the peak value of <img src=\"/media/7975dd3c6cb818c0536dcd8948bcfb4c25ce1a7d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is reduced by 10%, then average value of <img src=\"/media/19a0eabd75fd38d95be48bdf22cf2fca389c4983.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> becomes _____ mA.<br />\n(Rounded off to two decimal places)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/ec07fc2a88adbedd478838fccae7f792a666026d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"33.33","high":"33.33"},"solution":"<p>33.33 (32.50 - 34.50)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/c5a37593073fe4d07e5223d0926ddd93f9472f15.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the network given below total output swing voltage is ____V. (Assume RC to be very large)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/0df94ca1d5572f150e3797297df6d0a61e30dbe7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"40","high":"40"},"solution":"<p>40 (40 - 40)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/e6b6aa95d064389d704fa4fb7236b1b635fa59c8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/96ac6fe5af8b6429e265f9ac5f60b75ac1fab165.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the network shown below, <em>V<sub>L</sub></em> is to be maintained at 12 V for a load variation <img src=\"/media/2ad7fb1603cb6ce0442e4137d2cb213d11307808.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> from 0 to 200 mA. Then the value of <em>R<sub>S</sub></em> and VZ is given by</p>\n<p>(Assume the Zener diode to be ideal)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/0b4a04015b385b6a04b8cbb37ed36e2449b668cc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>V<sub>Z</sub></em> = 12 V, <em>R<sub>S</sub></em> = 20 Ω</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>V<sub>Z</sub></em> = 12 V, <em>R<sub>S</sub></em> = 10 Ω</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>V<sub>Z</sub></em> = 20 V, <em>R<sub>S</sub></em> = 12 Ω</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>V<sub>Z</sub></em> = 10 V, <em>R<sub>S</sub></em> = 12 Ω</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/26a696b538572669c34a489358ff86850e9b02f2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/53658b9eb4eb954a36248179bf64c84e1b37b027.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>For the network shown below, the range of <img src=\"/media/9d496b02862e5f6d0b7a20d49c70971d9d6f6455.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> that maintain <em>V<sub>L</sub></em> at 8 V and not exceed the maximum power rating of the Zener diode is</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/5abc0df0ee9b20b34a1b42a096299f4f93a7ffbf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 10.50 V to 12.20 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 8 V to 19 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 11.30 V to 15.85 V</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 10 V to 40 V</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/1113287995be77da00ae27d942